Digital and Netscape Communications expand their product portfolio

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Netscape products for Windows NT Alpha systems are now available from
   Digital

o  New versions of Netscape products now available from Digital

o  New Netscape News and Proxy Server software products now available from
   Digital

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital and Netscape Communications are releasing the next versions of their
client/server Internet software products. New versions of the popular
Netscape Navigator, Netscape Commerce Server, and Netscape Communications
Server, and the newly developed Netscape News Secure Server and Netscape
Proxy Server, give individuals and organizations advanced capabilities for
serving and managing online information and conducting business online. With
these offerings, Digital and Netscape Communications dramatically expand
their client/server open Internet software solutions for enabling
information exchange and electronic commerce on the Internet and corporate
TCP/IP networks.

The Netscape Navigator and Netscape Server product lines offer easy-to-use
interfaces for serving, accessing, and managing multimedia information on
the Internet, including formatted text, graphics, audio, and video. They
employ a hypertext linking system that lets users simply click on a word or
image to retrieve information wherever it is located on the network. The
products are also fully compatible with existing public domain versions of
NCSA's Mosaic software, making transitions to these commercial products
simple.

The Netscape Navigator now offers right-to-copy licenses. Users can purchase
one complete kit for any of the supported platforms, and buy right-to-copy
product packages of 10, 100, 500, 1,000, 2,000, 5,000, or 10,000. For
example, if an organization has a variety of platforms for which it needs
clients, it can purchase a single complete kit of each operating system type
and the right-to-copy package for the total number of clients. The
right-to-copy package is generic and non-operating system specific, so it
can support any full client kit.

Netscape products running on Digital's Alpha systems offer a significant
performance advantage over any other complete Internet solution available
today. When the number of users on a given network increases, Alpha systems
consistently outperform Intel and RISC systems in all performance tests.
This is an advantage for any organization that expects to expand its
network.

Organizations purchasing Netscape products from Digital can also take
advantage of one-stop Internet software shopping, which is becoming more and
more important in the ever-changing world of "Internetworking." Purchasing
Internet software products from strategic vendors such as Netscape
Communications through Digital is as easy as purchasing Digital's own
software products.

Netscape Communications' products provide corporate communications functions
that are most widely needed and used. Rich hypermedia documents in a variety
of document formats are quickly, easily, and securely distributed and
discussed. Because these products will function over any TCP/IP-based
network, including the corporate LAN or WAN and the Internet, they minimize
initial investments and cost of network operation for any organization.

Netscape Navigator V1.1

Netscape Navigator V1.1 serves as a drop-in replacement for all
HTTP-compliant network browsers. It interoperates with all common network
servers and provides:

o  Integrated capabilities and viewers that make all-in-one web browsing a
   reality.
o  Performance-focused design for rapid response.
o  Advanced interface design, which delivers state-of-the-art ease of use.
o  Multi-protocol built-in security, which ensures that private information
   is protected.
o  A common look, feel, and behavior across platforms.
o  New features including: tables; backdrops; client refresh; popups; secure
   news; remote control (X, Windows, and Macintosh) and OLE (Windows); SSL
   and proxies; Japanese; native AU/AIFF (Windows); content type compressed
   (UNIX); Netsite identification; ALT tag support; and bullet colors.

Netscape Commerce Server V1.1

The Netscape Commerce Server provides advanced security features, enabling
the expansion of web technology into a host of new applications both within
and beyond the enterprise. With this product, users can develop and safely
distribute marketing presentations or sales leads throughout the enterprise,
all around the world. They can also distribute new product plans and company
financial reports to a restricted audience within the company on a need to
know basis, or distribute marketing plans and product information securely
to partners and customers worldwide. Also, they can sell products and
services over the Internet. Whether used for communications over the
Internet or private TCP/IP-based networks, Netscape Commerce Server makes
secure electronic commerce and communications a reality.

The Netscape Commerce Server features data encryption, server
authentication, message integrity, and access authorization to ensure data
security. This integrated security system allows specified individuals or
groups to retrieve sensitive information on demand, or to transmit
confidential information such as account or credit card numbers.

The robust API in the Netscape Commerce Server also provides improved
process and memory management for unparalleled performance and reliability.
It delivers documents faster, its throughput is several times higher than
other HTTP servers, and its efficient process management minimizes system
load and increases reliability. This robust API allows dynamic extension of
server functionality and easy integration with various applications and
systems. And its easy-to-use graphical user interface software makes
installation and management simple and quick.

Netscape Commerce Server is secure, high-performance server software for
conducting secure electronic commerce and communications on the Internet and
other TCP/IP-based networks.

BENEFITS

o  Integrated security

   - Integrated security features are built for secure electronic commerce
     and communications.
   - Access authorization controls provide access to individual files or
     directories.
   - Advanced security features are provided using the open Secure Sockets
     Layer (SSL) protocol, which has been adopted by major vendors of
     Internet products, financial institutions, and certification
     authorities.
   - Certification, a third-party fee-based service, binds a server's public
     key to information about the owner of that key.

o  Open standards

   - Compliance with network standards and document formats facilitates
     communications with other environments and systems. The Netscape
     Commerce Server uses the open SSL protocol to provide encryption,
     authentication, and message integrity.

o  High performance serving

   - An innovative Mob Process Model in Netscape software delivers unmatched
     performance and efficiency, and improves process and memory management
     by eliminating unnecessary overhead requests. As a result, Netscape
     Commerce Server software delivers documents faster than other HTTP
     servers and delivers several times greater throughput.

o  Easy-to-use

   - QuickStart Installation uses Netscape Navigator forms to create an
     intuitive graphical user interface for the Netscape Commerce Server,
     enabling new users to get up and running in minutes. It also
     facilitates ongoing maintenance, such as creating and managing access
     authorization and reviewing access logs using the same intuitive
     interface.

o  Extensible functionality using CGI and NSAPI

   - The Common Gateway Interface (CGI) and the Netscape Server API (NSAPI)
     provide mechanisms for extending server functionality and
     interoperating with other systems.

Netscape Communications Server V1.1

The Netscape Communications Server is high performance, easy-to-use server
software for publishing rich hypermedia documents on the Internet and on
corporate networks. It addresses both the opportunities and the challenges
of networked communications, and its compliance with network standards and
document formats, combined with its robust API to other applications and
systems, extend communications capabilities both within and beyond the
enterprise.

The easy-to-use graphical user interface in Netscape Communications Server
software make installation and management simple and quick. Flexible access
authorization lets users determine who should have access to particular
resources and create domains of access across any network. Also, the modular
design and scaleable process model of the Netscape Communications Server
enables it to grow with the communications needs of the user community. The
Netscape Communications Server is critical for anytime, anywhere access to
information.

Documents come alive when delivered using the Netscape Communications Server
Hypermedia documentation feature. It combines industry standard multimedia
document formats -- which allow the presentation of rich text, graphics,
audio and video -- with easy-to-navigate hyperlinks. HTML hyperlinks and
native imagemaps link related information, creating a complex yet seamless
web of information across any domain.

BENEFITS

o  Open standards

   - Compliance with network standards and document formats facilitates
     communications with other environments and systems.

o  Easy-to-use

   - The Server Manager lets users perform ongoing maintenance, such as
     creating and managing access authorization, reviewing access logs, and
     managing processes using the same intuitive interface.

o  Flexible access control

   - Access authorization provides users with complete control over access
     to individual files, directories, or servers using a username and
     password, domain name, host name, IP address, and/or named groups. Its
     flexible mechanism for controlling user privileges enables the creation
     of domains of access across any network.

o  Extensible functionality using CGI and NSAPI

   - The Common Gateway Interface (CGI) and the Netscape Server API (NSAPI)
     provide mechanisms for extending server functionality and
     interoperating with other systems in the enterprise.

Netscape News Secure Server V1.1

Netscape News Secure Server and its advanced security features make
communicating through the Internet and internal news groups possible.
Working in concert with the Netscape Navigator (or any other SSL-compatible
newsreader), the Netscape News Secure Server can encrypt and decrypt its
communications to ensure that only specified users can access newsgroups.
This powerful communications tool can be used by a project team to manage
schedules, discuss feature tradeoffs, and collaborate with partners outside
the company. The sales force can use it to get updates on pricing, discuss
effective sales practices, and communicate with distribution partners.
Customer support groups can use newsgroups to manage user groups, reducing
the cost of support. The Netscape News Secure Server increases collaboration
and communication both within and beyond the enterprise.

Netscape News Secure Server is easy-to-use, secure server software that
accepts public Usenet news feeds and lets organizations create and maintain
secure, private newsgroups for distribution over the Internet or any other
TCP/IP-based network. It includes programs to retrieve, maintain, and send
articles, and its simple graphical user interface makes installation,
configuration, and maintenance of these programs quick and easy. Its
advanced security features include data encryption, server authentication,
message integrity, and access authorization. Also, Netscape News Secure
Server supports MIME-type attachments, allowing newsgroups to distribute
documents that include graphical formats.

BENEFITS

o  Open Standards

   - Adherence to existing standards ensures the widest possible range of
     communication and collaboration. It uses the standard Network News
     Transport Protocol (NNTP) and runs on any TCP/IP network.

o  Integrated security

   - Netscape provides integrity security features that greatly expand the
     powerful newsgroup communications capability to permit confidential
     business matters to be discussed online, both within the company and
     with partners or customers. Advanced security features are provided
     using the open Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) protocol.

o  Graphical attachments

   - Attaching documents in various graphical formats greatly expands the
     capability of a newsgroup to serve as a repository of information and
     knowledge. Colleagues can download documents sent to the group, mark
     them up, and send them back. Support for MIME attachments in Netscape
     News Secure Server lets users attach any number of common document
     formats and expand group collaboration into a rich and graphical world.

o  Easy-to-use

   - Setting up new users, getting and sending news feeds to and from remote
     servers, and implementing security takes minutes using the News
     Server's intuitive interface. Its online documentation provides
     real-time and context-sensitive help, eliminating the need to flip
     between help windows and production windows.

Netscape Proxy Server V1.1

The Netscape Proxy Server provides secure Internet access and increased
performance for corporate users behind a firewall. The server provides
high-speed caching of information, which reduces the overall network load
and increases response time for users requesting previously accessed data
from the Internet, thereby reducing the cost of an organization's link to
the Internet. Netscape Proxy Server provides transaction logging; users can
screen outbound network accesses, restrict various users, or restrict access
to certain information on the Internet.

SERVICES

A complete range of software support, update, and license subscription
services are available on a worldwide basis. Organizations have the option
to purchase Telephone Support Service, New Version License Subscription
Service, a packaged service that provides rights to use new versions and
updates to the software, and Documentation Update Distribution Service.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

All Netscape products listed above are available now. Each QB kit contains a
single CPU license, media, and hardcopy documentation. The X Windows kit
includes versions for Digital UNIX, HP-UX 9.03, IRIX 5.2, IBM AIX 3.2,
Solaris 1.0 and 2.3, or SunOS 4.1.3.

For right-to-copy packages, users must purchase a kit for every system on
which they plan to run the software. Right-to-copy licenses are
non-operating system specific.

