   and to implement more complex security policies if required

o  Is extremely competitive on price

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The high rate of Internet connectivity has raised an acute sense of the
danger involved in connecting to the Internet and the critical need for
network security. The Digital Firewall for UNIX software provides users with
security between their private networks and the Internet. It combines packet
filtering, trusted application gateways, comprehensive logging, and a GUI in
a pre-configured software package. The product is user-installable on a
Digital UNIX based Alpha workstation.

Digital's Firewall for UNIX pre-configured software provides the following
features:

o  Every packet of data that passes through the firewall is examined. If the
   packet does not conform to the security policy specified by the system
   administrator, it is rejected.

o  Trusted application gateways are used to provide access to a wide range
   of Internet services -- mail (SMTP), FTP, Telnet, news (NNTP), WWW, and
   Finger services. The product also provides an administrator-configurable
   generic gateway for user-specific (non-standard) services, and supports
   Hand Held Authentication (HHA).

o  The product automatically logs data generated by the firewall, and
   provides the administrator with the ability to select from a menu of
   report types detailing individual service usage over various periods. The
   product also provides a configurable alarm system so that the
   administrator is automatically alerted to security events. The alarm
   system will trigger both system and user supplied alarms, and will
   maintain a configurable firewall system security level supporting the
   shutdown of individual services or the complete firewall.

o  The product includes a graphical user interface (GUI) that supports
   everything from initial configuration and ongoing management and
   administration of the firewall to naming services and time stamping. As
   well as delivering ease of use, the interface implements an information
   design that allows it to act as an assistant to administrators, guiding
   them to configure and manage the firewall correctly. The firewall
   interface is HTML-based, with the product including an HTML document
   browser. Access is restricted to the administrator or other personnel
   authorized on the firewall system.

BENEFITS

o  The Digital Firewall for UNIX software provides reliable and secure
   access to vital Internet services, and prevents any unauthorized
   connection to or from the Internet.

o  The configuration of the firewall is flexible, allowing users to set and
   modify their own security policy. Access to Internet services can be
   extended or limited based on a site's needs.

o  The user's investment is protected since a user anticipating future
   expansion and growth can buy the product now and later re-configure it
   into a multi-CPU firewall configuration.

