Border Network Technologies' BorderWare Firewall Server V3.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Border Network Technologies Inc.'s BorderWare Firewall Server V3.0 is now
   available from Digital

o  This combined entry-level firewall and Internet server package is easy to
   install and run on a PC

o  It is ideal for small to medium size enterprises that want a prepackaged,
   plug-and-play Internet security and server product for PCs, Macs, and
   workstations

o  Special incentive pricing is available for VARs, and Evaluation Kits are
   available for end users

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Border Network Technologies Inc.'s BorderWare Firewall Server defines a new
firewall product category by combining packet filters and circuit-level
gateways with application servers in a single, highly secure, self-contained
system. It is a powerful, advanced security product that protects TCP/IP
networks from unwanted external access, and controls internal access to
external services.

Using the BorderWare Firewall Server V3.0, users can connect their private
TCP/IP networks to the global Internet or other external TCP/IP networks,
confident that unauthorized users cannot obtain access to systems or files
on their private networks.

The benefits and uses of BorderWare V3.0 go far beyond protecting a network
from external access. BorderWare software provides many application servers,
including secure mail, dual name (internal and external), news, anonymous
FTP, WWW, and Finger information servers.

BorderWare V3.0 is transparent to internal network users. This means that
all of the TCP/IP networking applications that an organization currently
uses, including MS-DOS and Windows driven software, will continue to work
exactly as they do now, without modification.

In the past, having a totally secure internal network meant limiting one's
external access. Network administrators had to find a balance between
acceptable risk and required network usage. With the BorderWare Firewall
Server, this is no longer the case. The user's internal network can be
completely secure without affecting access to the external network.

Simplicity

BorderWare V3.0 has a simple graphical user interface for configuration,
setup, and control of the firewall server. V3.0 enables users to configure
all aspects of the firewall through the GUI, including dual name servers,
mail, news, outbound access, WWW, FTP, and alarms. With V3.0, users can
enable their own user-defined services or allow the BorderWare product to do
it for them in a secure manner. Every BorderWare V3.0 capability is disabled
until the user explicitly enables it.

Security

Firewalls come in three types: packet filters, circuit-level gateways, and
application gateways. BorderWare V3.0 combines all three types into one
firewall server, giving users the flexibility and security they need.
BorderWare V3.0 also supports multiple styles of authentication, including
address and port based authentication and cryptographic authentication. All
of these features make for a very secure firewall.

BENEFITS

o  Is the lowest cost firewall for small to medium size enterprises.

o  Provides a one-stop solution to a secure Internet gateway.

o  Is easy to use; BorderWare V3.0 works with any PC, Mac, or UNIX Internet
   application.

o  Offers complete transparency to internal users; there is no need to
   change application software or user procedures.

o  Has everything needed to link to the Internet, incorporating application
   servers like mail, news, WWW, FTP, and dual name servers.

o  Makes joining the Internet easy; it remaps and hides all internal IP
   addresses, allowing use of non-registered IP addresses.

o  Is a complete network security solution that combines packet filtering
   with application- and circuit-level gateways.

o  Provides worry-free inbound access; authenticated inbound Telnet access
   is permitted using one-time password "tokens."

o  Offers flexibility; security administrators can define proxies for secure
   and specialized applications that require "tunneling" through the
   firewall.

o  Is easy to install and manage; BorderWare V3.0 provides a simple
   graphical interface for configuration, control, and set-up.

o  Lets the administrator know when the system is being attacked; security
