enVISN Architecture for Digital's Networking Products

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Combines virtual LAN technology, distributed routing, and high-speed
   switching with centralized, policy-based administration to create
   flexible virtual networks

o  Enables the management of the logical network topology, rather than just
   multiple individual networking components

o  Provides maximum flexibility in establishing virtual LANs

o  Offers One-Hop Switching, enabling the formation of high performance
   workgroup virtual LANs across switched networks

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

enVISN (enterprise Virtual Intelligent Switched Networks) is Digital's
network architecture that combines virtual LAN technology, distributed
routing, and high-speed switching with centralized, policy-based
administration to create flexible virtual networks that can be customized to
application and business needs. Digital's approach integrates hub,
switching, and routing functionality using standard protocols to deliver
flexible, secure, low-latency access to the full complement of network
services regardless of technology or physical location.

Digital's enVISN architecture enables network managers to:

o  Create virtual groups of users and network resources independent of the
   physical network topology.

o  Lower the cost and complexity of network management through centralized,
   policy-based administration and distributed intelligence.

o  Integrate remote and mobile users into the enterprise network by
   delivering LAN-like services to remote users.

o  Utilize current products to gain the benefits of switched virtual LANs
   today, while providing an easy, low-cost migration path to the full
   benefits of virtual networking tomorrow.

o  Create flexible virtual LANs from any combination of physical ports,
   Macintosh addresses, and subnet addresses across multiple technologies,
   including Ethernet, Token Ring, FDDI, and ATM.

o  Go beyond virtual LANs to implement virtual networks that provide the
   scalability and optimized inter-virtual LAN routing needed by today's
   dynamic organizations.

o  Provide a range of service policies, including secure workgroups, high
   performance One-Hop Switching, and bandwidth allocation, to fine tune the
   network to application and business requirements.

Digital now provides the complete core switching infrastructure for all
levels within the organization -- the desktop, the department, and the
enterprise. Digital is the only vendor shipping Ethernet, FDDI, and ATM
switching today, all within an integrated architecture and strategy.

Digital's enVISN products prepare networks for the role that ATM will have
in virtual networking by enabling the integration of legacy LANs and WANs
with ATM.

New products include:

o  DECswitch 400 -- A departmental switch that expands Digital's current
   virtual LAN capabilities from Ethernet-only virtual LANs to Ethernet
   virtual LANs that can span across ATM backbones. The DECswitch 400 is a
   standalone modular switch used to connect Ethernet stations or segments
   to ATM backbone networks. The DECswitch 400 supports up to 24 dedicated
   Ethernets, with one or two ATM ports. Used in conjunction with the DEChub
   900 MultiSwitch, it can connect enVISN class 1 virtual LANs in the hub
   over an ATM network. The DECswitch 400 supports ATM Forum LAN Emulation
   Client, User Network Interface (UNI) V3.0 and V3.1, Classical IP, and
   inter-virtual LAN IP routing.

   For more information, see the "DECswitch 400 Ethernet/ATM Switch" article
   in this issue.

o  GIGAswitch/ATM V1.3 software -- A free upgrade to continue Digital's
   commitment to full standards compliance with the ATM Forum. V1.3 adds ATM
   Forum-compliant LAN Emulation Server and UNI V3.1 to the GIGAswitch/ATM
   system, a high performance ATM switch ideally suited for use in local
   area networks and high performance workgroups. With enVISN, LAN emulation
   enables multiple existing LAN technologies to be combined in a single
   network with an ATM backbone.

o  DECNIS ATMcontroller 631 -- An aggressively priced ATM network interface
   card for the DECNIS 600 multiprotocol backbone router supporting T3, E3,
   and OC-3 connections. Delivering on its commitment to integrate
   traditional WANs with enVISN networks, this new card connects traditional
   wide area services, such as T1, Frame Relay, and SMDS, into an ATM
   backbone.

Digital is already delivering many key components of its enVISN
architecture. For example, the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch provides a flexible,
multi-gigabit platform for building switched virtual networks. Its unique
technology-independent backplane enables network managers to integrate
Ethernet, Token Ring, and FDDI today, as well as ATM and 100 MB Ethernet
tomorrow -- without requiring hardware upgrades or replacements. Digital
will continue to introduce new products within this same flexible chassis,
enabling users to realize the full benefits of the enVISN virtual
networking.

BENEFITS

Digital now offers a full line of frame and cell switches to satisfy the
complete range of performance and functionality requirements -- from desktop
to department to enterprise backbones. These switches ensure forward
migration from legacy shared LAN environments to high speed switched
solutions. Digital offers PORTswitch and DECswitch products for the desktop
and department. For the backbone, Digital's GIGAswitch family of high
performance enterprise switches delivers robust interconnection of
centralized server farms and campus backbones.

Digital's DEChub 900 MultiSwitch provides a high performance,
technology-independent, scalable platform to support today's traditional
Ethernet, Token Ring, and FDDI LANs, as well as new technologies such as 100
Mb per second Ethernet and ATM.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECswitch 400 is available now. GIGAswitch/ATM software is included in
the GIGAswitch/ATM system. Upgrades for existing users are free of charge.
V1.3 will be available in July 1995. The DECNIS ATMcontroller 631 will be
available in August 1995.




