POLYCENTER Security Console V1.0 for Windows

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides client/server capability for the central management of the
   POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager security tool on multiple OpenVMS
   nodes and clusters

o  Includes a Microsoft Windows easy-to-use graphical user interface (GUI)

o  Allows easy creation and distribution of multiple POLYCENTER Security
   Compliance Manager test inspectors to nodes and clusters

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

According to a recent F.B.I. report, information technology security
breaches are costing American businesses $3 to $5 billion per year.
Digital's comprehensive security product and service portfolio can provide
users with reliable, cost-effective solutions to security problems.

POLYCENTER Security Console V1.0 for Microsoft Windows is a security tool
that allows system or security managers to configure and manage the use of
the POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager for OpenVMS tool on multiple
nodes and clusters. V1.0 provides easy and effective management of the
security of large systems from a single PC location.

Users can employ the POLYCENTER Security Console GUI to create POLYCENTER
Security Compliance Manager test inspectors (a collection of tests) for
implementing a security policy. They can distribute the inspectors to nodes
running POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager; the inspectors run on the
nodes at the time specified by the user. Then, users can access inspection
reports and graphs from the POLYCENTER Security Console GUI.

Positioning Digital's POLYCENTER Security Products

The POLYCENTER Security Console addresses ease of use and central
management, adding a new dimension to Digital's security portfolio. The
product will be extended to cover other operating systems supported by the
Compliance Manager, such as Digital UNIX, IBM AIX, HP-UX, SunOS, Sun Solaris
2, and Novell NetWare software. Coupled with the POLYCENTER Security
Reporting Facility, POLYCENTER security tools provide a unique
enterprisewide management solution that addresses the needs of workgroups,
data centers, and global networks.

In addition to the POLYCENTER Security Console, the POLYCENTER security
products portfolio consists of:

o  POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager -- Formerly known as DECinspect
   Compliance Manager, this product set allows system managers to implement
   a baseline level of security in their networked computing environments.
   The first line of defense is to implement security policies across the
   network and ensure that all systems remain in compliance. Compliance
   Manager products address this need while reducing the overhead required
   to manage the network.

o  POLYCENTER Security Intrusion Detector -- This software provides realtime
   security monitoring to detect any suspicious or hostile activity caused
   by hackers or inexperienced users. It initiates counter-measures in
   response to potential security violations in realtime, and can notify
   system management personnel of the potential violations.

o  POLYCENTER Security Reporting Facility -- This facility consolidates
   enterprisewide security information for systems running either the
   POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager or the POLYCENTER Security
   Intrusion Detector -- making it possible to view current and historical
   information. The software supports a hierarchical reporting structure
   that combines data, allowing the building of a security management
   structure that fits the organization, regardless of its size.

BENEFITS

o  POLYCENTER Security Console meets user requirements for an easy-to-use,
   fast, and efficient security tool.

o  POLYCENTER Security Console represents a major improvement in efficiency
   in security management. The system manager now has a central point of
   control, and the product uses strong authentication to provide extra
   security when accessing the servers in the network.

o  POLYCENTER Security Console, when used in conjunction with the
   re-designed POLYCENTER Security Compliance Manager, enables users to
