DECnet/OSI V6.2 for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Enhances the capabilities of Digital's network transports

o  Choice of network transport and network naming service without
   modifications to existing network applications

o  NCL now easy to use

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECnet/OSI V6.2 for OpenVMS systems updates and enhances the capabilities of
Digital's network transports product set. It provides the ability for
network managers to choose their network transport and network naming
service without having to modify their existing network applications. All
licensed DECnet applications, along with user-written and third party DECnet
applications, can be run over NSP (DECnet transport protocol), CLNS or CONS
(OSI transport protocols), or TCP/IP transports. OSI applications, such as
FTAM, VT, X.400, and X.500, can be run over the OSI protocols or TCP/IP. The
ability to run these applications over TCP/IP is based on an extension to
RFC 1006, currently available from the IETF as an Internet Draft. Through
the use of open interfaces, DECnet/OSI V6.2 allows for the use of any TCP/IP
protocol stack available on OpenVMS systems.

Name service choices allow users to access naming information stored in a
larger local name service (now supporting up to 100,000 nodes per system),
DECdns, or DNS/bind.

Finally, NCL is now easy to use through the implementation of a Motif based
graphical network management interface.

DECnet/OSI software continues to preserve existing investments in network
hardware and applications. DECnet/OSI software is DECnet software plus OSI
software, making it fully compatible with DECnet Phase IV. Because the Phase
IV protocols have been preserved in DECnet/OSI V6.2, existing DECnet
applications will run unchanged on a DECnet/OSI system. DECnet/OSI and
DECnet Phase IV systems coexist transparently in a single network.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECnet/OSI V6.2 for OpenVMS systems is available now on the OpenVMS Alpha
and VAX CD-ROMs. Pricing is unchanged for this release.

A separate TCP/IP protocol stack is required to use the new DECnet software
over IP features. DECnet/OSI V6.2 has been tested with the TCP/IP products
from Digital, Process Software, the Wollongong Group, and TGV, Inc. Contact
the vendor for the appropriate product version.

A DECnet/OSI license gives the owner the right to use either DECnet/OSI or
DECnet Phase IV on OpenVMS systems. The DECnet/OSI license is frequently
included as part of VAX and Alpha system packages. Users who purchase those
system packages will receive the new V6.2 license. When a DECnet/OSI license
is not included with the system package, a separate license is required.

The End System license provides the right to use the base DECnet and OSI
protocol stacks, FTAM, VT, DECdns Clerk, DECdts, X.25 Access, and network
management. The Extended Function license provides all functions in the End
System license plus the OSI Application Gateways, Cluster Alias, and, on VAX
platforms, the DECdns Server.

Update Licenses

Users who already own a DECnet/OSI license need an update license to move to
V6.2. An update license can be obtained in the following ways:

o  Directly purchase the update license (price is about 30 percent of new
   license price).

o  As part of an existing Software Update Subscription License (SUSL)
   contract. SUSL is an annual contract that gives the owner rights to all
   new releases of software that come out during that year. Normally, the
   price is about 12 percent of the new license price per year.

The SUSL contract is included as part of some system service contracts, so
users with these contracts will be authorized to use DECnet/OSI V6.2. All
DECnet/OSI owners must purchase the update license or receive it as a part
of SUSL to use V6.2. Previous purchase of DECnet/OSI does not convey the
right to use new software versions.

Documentation is provided on CD-ROM. Hardcopy documents are also available.
New features for this release have been documented in the Release Notes.

