StorageWorks HSZ40 Array Controller Utility for Digital UNIX V1.1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  No-cost utility program allows Digital UNIX system administrators to
   configure HSZ40 array controllers using terminal windows on Digital UNIX
   systems

o  Eliminates the need for a terminal directly attached to the HSZ40 array
   controller

o  Full range of HSZ40 configuration and non-periodic monitoring commands

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The StorageWorks HSZ40 Array Configuration Utility for Digital UNIX
(formerly called DEC OSF/1) systems allows communication with HSZ40 array
controllers through a terminal window on a suitably privileged Digital UNIX
workstation. The window behaves as if it were a terminal attached directly
to the HSZ40 controller. All controller CLI commands except those that use
cursor positioning escape sequences are supported. For example, because
HSZterm is character-cell oriented, it cannot handle the VTDPY displays (the
periodic status displays emitted by the HSZ40) that include VT escape
sequences for cursor positioning.

System administrators are able to:

o  Manage any number of HSZ40 array controllers from a single workstation.
o  Manage any HSZ40 array controller attached to any Digital UNIX system
   with which they can establish a connection.
o  Use commands identical to those that would be used from a directly
   attached terminal (no new interfaces to learn).
o  Use the non-graphical monitoring facilities of the HSZ40 CLI to observe
   performance and status information.

BENEFITS

The HSZ40 array controller supports a variety of individual disk and disk
array configuration options in the Digital UNIX environment. These include
unit addressing, read and write caching, array member removal and
replacement, and others. Until now, configuring an HSZ40 array controller
has required that a terminal be attached directly to the controller. This is
not always convenient, particularly in large installations where the system
administrator is not close to the system or storage that is being
configured.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The StorageWorks HSZ40 Array Controller Utility is available now. There is
no license charge to those with Digital UNIX operating system licenses.
Media and documentation are included on the Consolidated Distribution for
Digital UNIX Layered Products.

SERVICES

No software services are available for the StorageWorks HSZ40 Array
Controller Utility.

TECHNICAL DATA

The StorageWorks HSZ40 Array Controller Utility works with all systems that
support the Digital UNIX operating system (V2.0, V3.0, or V3.2) and the
HSZ40 array controller. HSZ40 array controllers must be running the
StorageWorks HS Operating Firmware V2.0 or 2.5. In order to control stripesets or raidsets,
licenses for those functions must be installed on the controller.

