POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management V1.1 for OpenVMS

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Works with TL820 tape libraries

o  Compatibility with Media and Device Management Services (MDMS) allows
   libraries to be shared with POLYCENTER Archive Backup, Storage Library
   Services, and Sequential Media File software

o  Fewer licenses simplify pricing, and licensing is now based on how much
   space is freed when files are shelved

o  Remote device support allows OpenVMS systems to shelve to another cluster

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management for OpenVMS systems is a layered
software product that extends the OpenVMS file system to allow efficient
management of infrequently accessed (dormant) data.

V1.1 of the software features the following enhancements:

o  Integration with MDMS -- Allows POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage
   Management software to share TL820 tape libraries with other
   applications. TL810 libraries and STK silos, after they have been fully
   tested, will also be supported. MDMS also enables Hierarchical Storage
   Management to share robotic loaders, automatic tape libraries, drives,
   and scratch pools with POLYCENTER Archive Backup, Storage Library
   Services, and Sequential Media File software. In addition, MDMS allows
   users to employ arbitrary media labels instead of labels with required
   formats, such as the HSnnnn format.

o  New license support and pricing -- Fewer licenses simplify ordering, and
   a new "virtually unlimited" 999 TB license enables users to have
   virtually unlimited capacity -- enabling them to connect several TL820
   tape libraries for large capacity needs. Also, the storage capacity being
   used is now determined by how much online space is freed.

o  Remote device support -- Because the shelf server is now able to access
   remote devices, expensive tape devices and libraries can now be shared
   with nodes outside the OpenVMScluster system. In addition, OpenVMS
   systems are able to shelve files to other OpenVMScluster systems.

o  /VERIFY qualifier added to the BACKUP command -- With V1.1, policy can be
   defined that causes data to be shelved with a BACKUP/VERIFY operation,
   improving data integrity during shelving.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management V1.1 for OpenVMS systems (SPD
46.38) is available now through Digital and its business partners.

A flat priced structure is implemented for Traditional and Concurrent Use
Licenses. The software is priced on a per GB basis, based on the online
space that is freed.

Users are required to purchase a Hierarchical Storage Management Base
License for each cluster. The Base License provides unlimited use of the
product plus 20 GB of nearline storage capacity. The purchase of Concurrent
Use Licenses for incremental capacity is required, depending on the amount
of nearline storage (GB) that the Hierarchical Storage Management software
will manage.

For example:

o  A user who plans to use a full TZ877 library (140 GB) as a "shelf" will
   need to purchase a Base License plus six 20 GB Concurrent Use Licenses.

o  A user who plans to utilize 500 GB of a TL820 library (2.5 TB capacity,
   uncompressed) as a shelf for Hierarchical Storage Management will need to
   purchase a Base License plus a 500 GB Concurrent Use License.

o  A user who plans to use a full TL820 library (2.5 TB capacity,
   uncompressed) as a shelf will need to purchase a Base License plus a 999
   TB Concurrent Use License, which in effect provides unlimited storage.

Documentation kits are purchased separately. Volume discount "W" applies;
the product is non-discountable except to resellers.

