DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS Alpha Adds ACMS Support

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Operation with ACMS V4.0 on OpenVMS Alpha and OpenVMS VAX systems is now
   supported

o  Full set of DECforms development tools are now available on OpenVMS Alpha
   systems

o  DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS Alpha systems features the same functionality
   as DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS VAX systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The currently shipping ACMS (Application Control and Management System) V4.0
for OpenVMS Alpha systems and DECforms V1.4 for OpenVMS Alpha systems are
not compatible. Consequently, user configurations have been restricted to
OpenVMS VAX front-end systems using DECforms V1.4 and ACMS V3.3 or V4.0; or
OpenVMS Alpha servers using ACMS V4.0.

Also, DECforms V1.4 for OpenVMS Alpha systems contains only a subset of the
DECforms development environment -- requiring the user to have an OpenVMS
VAX system to do interactive development.

The new DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS Alpha systems supports ACMS V4.0 and the
complete set of DECforms development tools, eliminating the limitations of
V1.4.

In addition, DECforms V2.1 supports:

o  Motif GUI, including a VT-to-pixel layout converter
o  High quality forms printing on PostScript printers
o  Batch printing of forms
o  Multi-line text fields

Note also that DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS Alpha systems includes the new
"Guide to Developing an Application."

DECforms V2.1 for OpenVMS VAX systems supports ACMS V4.0 and includes a
number of software fixes. With V2.1, the VAX and Alpha versions of the
DECforms software are synchronized, and the SPDs for these versions are
combined into SPD 29.90.

BENEFITS

Users can now complete the migration of their computing systems and DECforms
plus ACMS based applications from VAX, or mixed VAX and Alpha,
configurations to entirely Alpha configurations.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECforms V2.1, both for OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS Alpha systems, is available
now through Digital, its DECdirect service, its U.S. Software Loan Program
(30, 60, 90, and 120 day loans), and its distributors.

To run DECforms V2.1 with ACMS V4.0, users will need to obtain and install
ACMS V4.0 and ECO (Engineering Change Order) number two, which will bring
the ACMS revision level to ACMS V4.0-2. The ECO, formally known as
"ACMSE02040," has been added to the currently shipping ACMS V4.0 kit and is
also available on the May 1995 Consolidated Distribution CD-ROM. Users with
support contracts can obtain ACMSE02040 from a local Customer Support Center
(CSC).

