DECdocument V2.3 for OpenVMS VAX Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides fixes for known problems in VAX DOCUMENT V2.2

o  100 percent compatible with DECdocument for OpenVMS AXP V2.3

o  Individual CD-ROM kit replaces retiring TK50 and 1600 BPI magtape media
   distribution

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Touch Technologies' DECdocument for OpenVMS VAX Systems V2.3 (SPD 27.55.xx)
is a style-based, document composition system using a device-independent
generic markup language. It automates the production of large,
format-intensive technical documentation. The markup tags have no specific
formatting information. DECdocument (formerly VAX DOCUMENT) software stores
the markup tags in a separate file, making it easy to support multiple
output formats for a single document.

BENEFITS

o  A wide variety of output types (Bookreader, HELP, PostScript, and text)
   is provided.

o  Plans for future releases of DECdocument include HTML (Hypertext Markup
   Language) and RTF (Rich Text Format) output.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECdocument V2.3 is available now. The TK50 and 1600 BPI magtape media
distribution is being retired with this release of DECdocument for OpenVMS
VAX software and replaced by an individual CD-ROM kit; it is also available
on the OpenVMS VAX Consolidated Software Distribution.

Service users who have Media and Documentation Distribution Services (MDDS)
contracts for TK50 and 1600 BPI magtape will receive the V2.3 update on
their current media; new sales will be on CD-ROM only.

