DEC COBOL V2.2 for Alpha Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Availability of DEC COBOL V2.2 for OpenVMS Alpha systems

o  Availability of DEC COBOL V2.2 for Digital UNIX systems

o  High compatibility with VAX COBOL for OpenVMS VAX systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

With DEC COBOL V2.2 for Alpha systems, users of VAX COBOL based applications
can now gain the power, speed, and expandability of Alpha systems. OpenVMS
users can employ DEC COBOL V2.2 for OpenVMS Alpha systems, while users who
need an ANSI-compliant COBOL solution can use DEC COBOL V2.2 for Digital
UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) systems.

DEC COBOL V2.2 provides a high performance native ANSI-85/89 high-level
COBOL compiler, with flagging extensions as specified in FIPS (Federal
Information Processing Standard) Publication 21-3. these extensions are
available on both the OpenVMS Alpha and Digital UNIX versions of the
software. Also, DEC COBOL produces high performance object code that can be
linked with the system "linkers" and the DEC COBOL Runtime Library (RTL)
software to support the building of COBOL applications.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DEC COBOL V2.2 for OpenVMS Alpha systems (SPD 45.92.04) and DEC COBOL V2.2
for Digital UNIX systems (SPD 51.16.03) are available now through Digital
and its DECdirect service (1-800-DIGITAL).

