DEC MLS+ V3.1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Enhanced binary compatibility with Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) and
   improves the ease of porting commercial off-the shelf applications for
   the secure UNIX environment

o  Trusted Network Information Service (NIS) support

o  Improved Windows interface

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Today's business and government environments often demand enhanced security
to protect valuable assets. Data assets are becoming more vulnerable because
of the increased use of distributed client/server computing. As risks
increase, user demands for integral security are increasing. Enhanced
operating system security is mandatory in a variety of markets preventing
unauthorized access to highly valuable, sensitive, classified, and/or
proprietary data.

DEC MLS+ V3.1 is a maintenance release of Digital's trusted UNIX operating
system software that includes several key new features:

o  Support for AlphaServer 2100 uniprocessors, as well as the full line of
   DEC 3000 processors.

o  Trusted NIS support - a distributed data lookup service for sharing
   information between systems on a network and allowing users to update
   their NIS passwords from an NIS DEC MLS+ V3.1 client.

o  SVR4-compatible streams.

o  Full TSIX(RE) 1.0 Network Security Compliance - a secure networking
   product based on the security protocols from the Trusted System
   Interoperability Group (TSIG). This compliance allows interoperability
   with other vendors supporting this protocol, such as Sun and HP.

o  Trusted remote printing - printers may be connected through a LAT or
   through a TCP/IP network.

o  Configurable window security label display - users now have control over
   which security labels are displayed in their window security banners, and
   they can choose to display either the information label and/or the
   sensitivity label or neither label; contraints are set by the Information
   System Security Officer.

o  Dynamic visuals support - the X server's default visual is dynamic
   (PseudoColor) and supports a multilevel security policy.

BENEFITS

DEC MLS+ V3.1 (SPD 46.21.01) provides the increased security UNIX users are
demanding. DEC MLS+ V3.1 Trusted UNIX Operating System is a
security-enhanced version of UNIX that provides both client and server
support for Alpha AXP servers and workstations.

DEC MLS+ V3.1 includes not only security enhancements to the Digital UNIX
kernel, but also security-enhanced versions of the industry standard
OSF/Motif V1.2.2 Window Manager and the X11 R5 Window Server. DEC MLS+ V3.1
is designed to meet the B1/CMW levels of security that go beyond the C2
security included in base DEC OSF/1 V2.

DEC MLS+ V3.1 uses the same security model as ULTRIX MLS+ and provides an
easy upgrade for existing ULTRIX MLS+ V2.0 users. Since the DEC MLS+
operating system expands upon the C2 security features in Digital UNIX
(formerly DEC OSF/1), it offers an excellent choice for any UNIX users
seeking a more secure environment.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DEC MLS+ V3.1 is now available for the DEC 3000 family and the AlphaServer
2100 uniprocessor.

The correct Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) user license is a prerequisite
for ordering MLS+ V3.1 licenses.

