Baan Company's TRITON V3.1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Comprehensive enterprise resource management system for the manufacturing
   industries

o  Multi-company, multi-site, multi-language, and multi-currency
   capabilities

o  Supports the hybrid manufacturer with built-in flexibility

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

TRITON, from the Baan Company, with dual headquarters in Ede, the
Netherlands, and Menlo Park, California, is a comprehensive enterprise
resource management system that meets the functional and technical demands
for the manufacturing industry. With its multi-company, multi-site,
multi-language, and multi-currency capabilities, TRITON supports the
international requirements to operate in a global market. Its strength is in
supporting the hybrid (mixed mode) manufacturer with built-in flexibility
for design-to-order, make-to-order, make-to-stock, and repetitive style of
manufacturing. This product is ideal for companies that are component
suppliers to the automotive, aerospace, defense, electronics, and the
general discrete industries.

TRITON includes the following modules:

o  TRITON Tools
o  TRITON Enterprise
o  TRITON Manufacturing
o  TRITON Distribution
o  TRITON Finance
o  TRITON Transportation
o  TRITON Project
o  TRITON Orgware

It is written utilizing the 4GL development environment TRITON Tools. TRITON
is a true client/server architecture supporting one, two, and three tier
client/server structures in a LAN or WAN environment. This architecture is
compliant with Digital's style of client/server computing and is the ideal
business solution for AlphaServer systems running the Digital UNIX (formerly
called DEC OSF/1) operating system. Clients may be conventional character
based terminals, X terminals, and PCs running Windows. Comprehensive help
facilities are available online. Maintainable security and access control
features protect sensitive data from unauthorized access.

One of the key design principles of TRITON is to provide an integrated
database utilizing a common data model for all modules of the TRITON set of
business applications. This common data model ensures that data from any
transaction within the TRITON set of functions is stored consistently in
realtime according to the model. This also ensures access to good
information that is timely, reliable, accessible, and understandable
throughout the enterprisewide computing environment.

The implementation of the common data model supports multiple relational
database management systems such as ORACLE, INFORMIX, SYBASE (under
development), and Baan's own databases, TRITON Base and TRITON Base TP. This
support provides for large and true distributed databases even in a
heterogeneous and distributed database environment.

The implementation of TRITON is supported by TRITON Orgware, a set of
software tools and methodology that allows for a smooth and successful
implementation. The implementation methodology is supported by TRITON Target
and TRITON IT-Services, making the implementation of software, hardware, and
orgware completely manageable.

The overall objective of these system supported services is to ensure an
implementation in the shortest amount of time with the least interruption to
the existing organization and a fast return on investments. TRITON
IT-Services bundles eight system supported service packages, from
orientation to the performance monitoring and tuning of the TRITON suite of
business applications. These services form the means by which users attain
the stages of the methodology of TRITON Target.

TRITON Product Family

o  TRITON Tools -- A powerful 4GL development kit for creating new
   applications and modifying existing applications; open to various
   standards on communications, databases, operating systems, and user
   interfaces; equipped with powerful tools to develop, document, translate,
   and maintain software applications.

o  TRITON Enterprise -- Management tool to improve business performance.
   TRITON Enterprise has been developed to provide accurate information on
   business performance -- delivered directly to managers.

o  TRITON Manufacturing -- A hybrid solution for engineer-to-order,
   assemble-to-order, and make-to-stock manufacturing environments. It comes
   with enhanced multi-site MRP II, product configurator, project control,
   and critical path activity analysis, as well as covering repetitive and
   job shop production and supply chain control for multi-site
   manufacturing.

o  TRITON Distribution -- A fully integrated logistics system with sales and
   purchase control, including contract management, inventory and location
   control, multi-level lot control and tracking, as well as electronic data
   exchange and integrated distribution requirements planning.

o  TRITON Finance -- Comprises general ledger, accounts payable and
   receivable, cash management, electronic and other payments and receipt
   methods, plus advanced budgeting with drill down facilities,
   activity-based costing, fixed assets, and multiple company consolidation
   and reporting.

o  TRITON Transportation -- Manages external logistics and transport for
   dedicated transport companies and companies organizing their own
   logistics. It provides transport order management, public warehousing,
   inventory control, vehicle and fuel administration, freight cost
   maintenance, load planning, and distribution requirements planning.

o  TRITON Project -- Provides integrated management of multiple projects,
   with project estimating; enhanced project planning with base, milestone
   and hammock activities; and project requirements. It also tracks progress
   against planning and estimates, including forecasts, invoicing, and
   result calculation.

o  TRITON Organizer -- Tools have been created to support the task of
   translating business processes and organizational requirements into the
   TRITON settings and configurations. For fast and easy implementation of
   TRITON, a business procedures organizer, implementation assistant, and
   multimedia toolkit are provided.

BENEFITS

o  Multiple manufacturing methods (hybrid) allow users to easily adopt their
   manufacturing strategy; these methods react quickly to changing business
   requirements.

o  A rule-based configurator allows the use of standard products with
   multiple and customized options -- from order bidding to manufacturing to
   distribution.

o  Extensive management information system utilizes the enterprisewide
   TRITON database with more than 80 predefined views of information. The
   information is presented by navigating through fish-bone diagrams. The
   views and information can be easily customized and extended.

o  Inventory is reduced due to strong support of the JIT manufacturing
   methodology.

o  Overhead costs are reduced due to a full integration of all TRITON
   modules. This tight integration ensures data reliability, consistency,
   and security throughout the entire system.

o  True, efficient, and transparent manufacturing cost control is maintained
   through activity based costing.

o  Comprehensive functionality is supplied, in particular for the hybrid
   (mixed mode) manufacturer, with strong support for multi-company,
   multi-site, multi-language, and multi-currency capabilities. This
   functionality strongly supports the international requirements for
   globally operating companies.

o  MRP II functions have extended simulation capabilities and graphical
   presentation of the planned activities.

o  Strong support for the design-to-order manufacturer is provided through a
   highly functional and fully integrated project control capability.

o  True one, two, and three tier client/server architecture and an
   easy-to-learn graphical user interface (Windows and X terminals) are
   provided.

o  Proven and efficient computer supported methodology and services allow
   for a fast implementation without major interruption to the implementing
   company and organization, translating into a fast return on investments.

o  Easy integration to other business systems, thus protecting past
   investments.

o  Worldwide support is provided through Baan offices in more then 35
   countries. This support includes a telephone hotline and dial-in
   services.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

TRITON V3.1 is available now through the Baan Company.

