DEC C and DEC C++ V5.0 for OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS Alpha Systems

DEC C and DEC C++ V5.0 for OpenVMS VAX systems, and DEC C and DEC C++ V5.0
for OpenVMS Alpha systems are new maintenance releases.

DEC C V5.0 for OpenVMS VAX systems and DEC C V5.0 for OpenVMS Alpha systems
contain fixes to known software errors, plus:

o  Substantial improvements to the /Standard=Common function (K&R standard
   compatibility mode).
o  Support for the XPG4 features of the Runtime Library, which will be
   provided with OpenVMS V6.2 for VAX and Alpha systems.
o  Multi-purpose compiles producing preprocessor output in conjunction with
   object modules, when requested.
o  Pre-defined macro compiler version numbers.
o  New preprocessor with improved K&R standard compatibility and robustness.
o  Merged front-end sources allowing consistency with other DEC C compilers
   on other Digital platforms.
o  Support for the digraph function as part of the ISO C addendum.

In addition, DEC C for OpenVMS Alpha systems includes:

o  Inline assembly language code that is compatible with the DEC C compiler
   for Digital UNIX (acc_cc) software, allowing multiple machine
   instructions and PAL calls without the introduction of built-in
   functions.
o  Support for OpenVMS V6.2
o  64-bit constants
