Digital Alpha VME 2100

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Both 190 MHz and 275 MHz CPU models of Digital Alpha VME SMP systems are
   now available
*  New name, pricing, and order numbers replace the AlphaServer 2100 4/190
   VME systems
*  High Performance, scalable SMP system supports a variety of VME and PCI
   options
*  Three PCI and five VME64 industry-standard I/O slots for user options

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital Alpha VME 2100 system is a variation of the AlphaServer  2100
systems. Designed for realtime and embedded  applications, the Alpha VME
2100 offers the popular VME64 I/O bus in place of the EISA bus that is part
of other AlphaServer 2100 systems. It offers users the flexibility to choose
from over 4,000 existing VMEbus options and combine them with high
performance PCI options in one integrated rackmountable system package. It
has CPU, memory, and standard I/O features and  functionality that
are identical to standard AlphaServer 2100 systems. The Alpha VME 2100
offers 19-inch rackmount packaging for versatility and reduced footprint;
and runs the Digital UNIX and OpenVMS operating systems.

Previously, the product was named the AlphaServer 2100 4/190 VME and was
available only with 190 MHz microprocessors. Now the product is offered in
both 275 MHz an d190 MHz models. Also, it has been renamed the Alpha VME
2100 to more clearly reflect the VME embedded system.

Users who can benefit from using the Alpha VME 2100 include:

*  Those who want the power and convenience of an Alpha four-CPU SMP system
   with symmetric multiprocessing software.
*  Those who want to use Alpha systems but also want to use abundant and
   inexpensive VME options for special I/O requirements.
*  Those who want to migrate their existing VMEbus computing systems to a
   more powerful platform but do not want to redesign their VME I/O modules.
*  Those who require a rackmount system to go with NEBS (Network Equipment
   Building Standard) compatible packaging in a 24-inch deep cabinet.

The Alpha VME 2100 can be ordered in either a horizontal slide-out drawer
configuration for space efficiency, or a vertical configuration for ease of
access and service.

BENEFITS

The Alpha VME 2100 system offers users the high performance and
price/performance of an Alpha  symmetric multiprocessing computer, directly
interfaced to the VMEbus, for use in today complex, compute intensive
realtime and embedded applications.

Symmetric multiprocessing offers computational capability that is
significantly more efficient and easier to program than the traditional
method of designing VME systems with multiple loosely-coupled single board
computers. Because the Alpha VME 2100 system uses a private, very high speed
internal bus for CPU to memory I/O, the VMEbus and the PCI are utilized only
for I/O operations -- resulting in a balanced system design.

The Alpha VME 2100 system offers both the versatility of VME and the high
performance of the new PCI bus; users no longer have to choose between
performance and versatility. Both PCI and VME options can be used together
in the same system package. High capacity is the hallmark of the Alpha VME
2100 system. Users can configure the Alpha VME 2100 system with up to 4
CPUs, up to 1GB of memory, and 4 GB of internal disk storage -- providing
high capacity and flexibility in a standard system cabinet. External disk
and additional expansion VME I/O cages can be rackmounted above or below
the system box.

The ability to configure the Alpha VME 2100 system with up to 1 GB of
physical  memory  means that applications that manipulate very large data
items --  such as graphical images, radar signals, or realtime  databases --
can  now perform the calculations directly in memory without time-
consuming disk I/O.

Over 4,000 VMEbus options from hundred of vendors are can be used with the
Alpha VME 2100; users simply plug them directly into the integral VME64 I/O
card cage included in the system. For expansion beyond  the five slots,
which are standard with the system, a PCI to VME bridge option is available
to connect the system to external VME card cages from any vendor in the VME
industry.

The Alpha VME 2100 system supports both the Digital UNIX and OpenVMS
operating systems, which offer realtime features for building embedded and
realtime applications. The VMEbus interface is supported on both operating
systems. Also, the applications programming interface for the internal PCI
to VME64 bridge and external PCI to VME adapter are the same, so porting I/O
devices among systems involves no software modifications.

Product positioning

The Alpha VME 2100 multiprocessing system is the high-end member of
Digital's  family  of VME products and can handle the most demanding
computational tasks. The AXPvme-64 and AXPvme-160 single board computers
provide the traditional VME board-level products.

The Alpha VME 2100 system complements the standard pedestal and rackmount
AlphaServer 2100 systems, which are configured with the EISA I/O bus
internally. The first Alpha SMP system designed specifically for the
embedded and realtime market, the Alpha VME 2100 system offers VMEbus
connectivity and symmetric multiprocessing in one integrated package. The
system shares all of the CPU, memory, and standard I/O components of the
AlphaServer 2100 family of servers. The Alpha VME 2100 system is designed
for VME technology users. If a user wants both PCI and EISA options, the
AlphaServer 2100 provides a solution for those needs.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital Alpha VME 2100 system is available now. It is factory installed
with either OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 or Digital UNIX V3.2; and can be ordered in
either a horizontal, slide-out drawer configuration or a vertical
configuration. Systems ship with a plain metal cover; dress front covers
(bezels) must be ordered separately if they are desired for a finished
appearance. Also,a keyboard and mouse are not included in the packaged
systems.

The Alpha VME 2100 systems are supported worldwide by Digital's service
organization, and supplemental servicescan be purchased to provide extended
service coverage.
