Rackmount VAX 4000

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Model 106A delivers a 20 percent performance improvement over the VAX
   4000 Model 105A
*  Rackmount Advantage Server packages offer memory, a 1.6 GB DSSI disk, an
   RRD43 CD-ROM, and OpenVMS VAX and NAS 200 software
*  Packages come with a three-year hardware warranty replacing the existing
   one-year warranty

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Rackmounting provides a cost effective way to organize systems, storage, and
other options in an easily accessible, 19-inch-wide EIA/ANSI standard
rackmount cabinet.  Rackmount configurations are ideally suited for
environments in which a minimum hardware footprint is required.  The
Rackmount VAX 4000 Model 106A requires only 8.75 inches of vertical rack
space.  Models 505A and 705A require only 14 inches of vertical rack space.
Cooling is from front to back to maximize usable cabinet space.

The Rackmount VAX 4000 Model 106A combines the power of a 10ns (nanosecond)
NVAX CMOS-4 processor, and all the features of the desktop VAX 4000 Model
106A, in a space-saving rackmountable configuration. It delivers a 20
percent performance increase over the Model 105A, which it replaces.

Rackmount VAX 4000 Models 106A, 505A, and 705A are now offered with a new
three-year hardware warranty which replaces the existing one-year warranty
and reduces the cost of maintenance over three years. Advantage Server
packages offer memory, a 1.6 GB DSSI disk, a RRD43 CD-ROM, and OpenVMS VAX
and NAS 200 software.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The VAX 4000 Model 106A and other Advantage Server packages will be
available in June.Installation is no longer included in the standard price,
but can be purchased separately.
Discount Codes: End User = Y, OEM = Q.

