   RISC platforms.
*  Support for OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 and OpenVMS VAX V6.1
*  Licensing and pricing change for OpenVMS server
   components

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER Scheduler V2.1B (SPD 32.19.05) provides users with automated
process scheduling functions, the ability to reschedule repetitive
jobs automatically, and synchronization of dependent jobs across
the network and heterogeneous platforms.  With its client/server
configuration, POLYCENTER Scheduler software supports the option for
users to centralize and localize the management of remote production
processing in a cost effective manner, as well as provide automated error
recovery and notification of job status.

New features

*  Agent support for OpenVMS Alpha, OpenVMS VAX, Windows
   NT Intel, HP-UX, and SunOS platforms
*  Support for OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 and OpenVMS VAX V6.1
*  New client/server licensing and pricing scheme
*  Software fixes

Please see the updated SPD (32.19.05) for details on product
components and key functionality.

BENEFITS

Users today are faced with managing multivendor systems across the wide
area network, and doing so cost effectively and efficiently without
increasing their human resources.  A key requirement for managing system
resources used for production processing is an automated job scheduling
system, such as POLYCENTER Scheduler software. POLYCENTER Scheduler
V2.1B optimizes the available CPU usage, synchronizes the dependency
processing across platforms and networks, and provides these features
in a cost effective configuration.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The POLYCENTER Scheduler V2.1B product components will be available
July 10 through Digital, its resellers and distributors, and the
