DEC ADA V3.2 For OpenVMS VAX Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

*  ISO Math Library support
*  8-Bit (Latin-1) character support
*  New Ada package
*  X11R4 and X11R5 bindings upgrade

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Ada programmers and application developers need a robust,
high-performance language for realtime and embedded systems.
Additionally, they need a production-quality, standards-
compliant language that reduces software costs by increasing
maintainability, evolvability, reliability, and portability
across multiple platforms.

DEC Ada software is Digital's high-performance, production-quality
compiler. It is a fully validated implementation of the full
ANSI/MIL-STD-1815A-1983 Ada Language. As a result of meeting the
ANSI standard, DEC Ada software also conforms to the Federal
Information Processing Standard (FIPS-119) and the International Standards
Organization (ISO/8652-1987) standards for Ada programming languages.

The DEC Ada compiler provides a modular structure for programs by
allowing separate compilation of program units; and by providing strong
typing, tasking, exception handling,and other standard language features
that are supported across implementations. DEC Ada V3.2 provides highly
optimized code for running on OpenVMS VAX systems, and a number of
features that make the compiler suitable for a variety of general and
realtime applications.

DEC Ada V3.2 features

*  Supports the ISO Math Library packages,
   GENERIC_PRIMITIVE_FUNCT and GENERIC_ELEMENTARY_FUNCTIONS.
*  Implements AI-00866, which permits an 8-bit character
   set based on ISO standard 8859/1 (commonly known as Latin-1).
*  New pre-defined library package contains the package
   numerics fashioned after the Ada.Numerics package in the
   Ada'95 standard.
*  Provides updated X11R4 and X11R5 bindings.
*  Includes miscellaneous software fixes.

DEC Ada V3.2 Professional Development Option

The DEC Ada Professional Development Option (PDO) is a separately
licensed option that is currently available with DEC Ada V3.2 for OpenVMS
VAX systems. Ada programmers need not change any of their development
procedures to benefit from the DEC Ada Professional Development Option.

It features:

*  Smart recompilation -- Significantly reduces the number
   of recompilations that are needed to rebuild a DEC Ada
   program after compilation units have changed, eliminating up
   to 100 percent of the usual recompilations.
*  Program library file-block caching -- Minimizes the
   actual amount of disk input and output that must be
   performed by using an in-memory cache of file blocks,
   significantly reducing the elapsed time for compilations.
*  Multilevel program library directory structure --
   Provides a more efficient program library directory
   structure to improve access to large program libraries.

BENEFITS

Hosted and targeted across several Digital hardware and software platforms,
the DEC Ada compiler enables software developers to create high quality
applications quickly and efficiently within a comprehensive development
environment. As a native-mode language, it is also well integrated with
the services and utilities available on OpenVMS Alpha, OpenVMS VAX, and
Digital UNIX (formerly known as DEC OSF/1) host systems. DEC Ada V3.2
provides a highly reliable, standards-based, quality Ada compilation system.
By remaining true to the Ada language standard, DEC Ada V3.2 provides the
same look and feel across multiple platforms and maintains a high degree
of application portability.

In V3.2, the software development environment is enhanced by the latest
release of DECset software (V12.0) for OpenVMS VAX systems -- a developer's
tool set that addresses traditional (3GL) programming needs in
cross-platform, integrated development environments. With DECset software,
DEC Ada users now have a programming tool set that supports software
developers' coding, debugging, testing, and maintenance activities.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DEC Ada V3.2 for OpenVMS VAX systems is available now through Digital and
its DECdirect service (1-800-DIGITAL). The DEC Ada compiler is also
available for OpenVMS Alpha and Digital UNIX systems.

The Read Before Installation Letter (QA-0VQAA-GZ) must be ordered (at no
cost) with all licenses of the DEC Ada Professional Development Option for
OpenVMS VAX systems.

The DEC Ada Professional Development Option binaries are provided with the
DEC Ada binaries on the Layered Product CD-ROM. Purchase of a DEC Ada
Professional Development Option for OpenVMS VAX Systems License
(QL-0VQA*-**) enables use of this capability.

Documentation for the DEC Ada Professional Development Option is provided in
Chapter Five of the Developing Ada Programs on OpenVMS Systems manual.

Note that the EDS-Scicon XD Ada cross-platform compilers for the Motorola
family of microprocessors and MIL-STD-1750A targets are still available for
OpenVMS VAX systems. These cross-platform compilers are designed for use in
embedded systems, generating optimized and relocatable code for the
aforementioned targets. For additional information, contact Cathy Axel, DEC
Ada product manager (see "Contacts"); or Alistair Wilson, XD Ada product
manager at EDS-Scicon, (617) 273-3030.

