Firefox's NOV*IX For Internet V1.0

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Digital and Firefox sign marketing agreement
*  NOV*IX for Internet available from Digital
*  Search, text retrieval, and content management software

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Firefox, Inc., located in San Jose, California, and Digital have entered
into a marketing partner agreement that will make Firefox software products
available from Digital. Firefox solutions provide server-based
internetworking solutions for the Novell NetWare environment.  These
solutions provide efficient and manageable communications for centralized
administration, security, and dynamic IP address management.

Firefox gives NetWare Windows users access to the world with its NOV*IX for
Internet product. NOV*IX for Internet provides popular Internet-cruising
applications that are integrated with NOV*IX.  These applications include
NCSA Enhanced Mosaic from Spyglass, Gopher utilities, E-Mail client, and a
Newsreader interface.

NOV*IX for Internet V1.0 provides:

*  Server-based TCP/IP -- NOV*IX for Internet installs as a NetWare Loadable
   Module (NLM) on a NetWare server or multi-protocol router. Its
   server-based TCP/IP keeps IPX/SPX at the workstation, requiring no
   additional workstation setup or configuration. When users want to
   connect, they merely log in as a NOV*IX client on the server.
*  Concurrent user licensing -- Every NOV*IX product is licensed by
   concurrent users, so any NetWare client assigned access privileges can
   utilize all of the services provided by a given NOV*IX NLM.  Telnet, FTP,
   Novell's LAN WorkPlace,and Internet services can be available to all
   privileged users.
*  Fire*Wall security -- A NOV*IX Fire*Wall provides security for both
   incoming and outgoing traffic with three integrated functions.

   - Host connect security, which creates a firewall between
     host resources and network users, limiting host access to
     authorized users or groups of users.
   - Remote connect security, which allows administrators to
     tightly restrict incoming traffic by allowing access only to
     specific FTP or Web servers, or by allowing access to
     specific IP addresses.
   - Internet connect security, which resolves business issues that arise
     when users have unlimited access to the Internet by controlling
     outgoing access to Internet hosts.

To use NOV*IX, a user must be authorized and logged in as a NetWare server
client. Tight NetWare integration allows a network administrator to manage
only one set of security objects for NetWare logins and TCP/IP
communications.NOV*IX clients are subject to all NetWare security checks,
including passwords, allowed login times, and intruder detection and
lockout.

BENEFITS

Security -- NOV*IX for Internet gives users fast, easy, secure access to the
Internet and TCP/IP services on demand. Using integrated NOV*IX tools,
management features, and Fire*Wall security, administrators can better
manage their resources by keeping all applications and administration at
the server.

*  Flexibility -- NOV*IX easily accommodates LAN growth, adding users and
   changes to LAN configuration by dynamically addressing workstations.  IP
   address conservation is also possible because NOV*IX allows
   administrators to choose client address configurations and assign shared,
   pooled, or conventionally fixed IP addresses, differentiating users by
   port number when addresses are shared.
*  Ease of implementation -- No knowledge of UNIX is required to implement
   NOV*IX for Internet, and centralized setup, installation, and management
   of client communications on the NetWare server eliminates the complexity
   of implementing standalone TCP/IP on individual workstations.
*  Controlled access -- Administrators can specify user traffic and can
   restrict Internet usage to essential business service network addresses.
   For example, a school may want to give teachers unlimited Internet access
   to museum hosts,  while limiting access for children.
*  Opportunity -- Gives users in a NetWare environment access to the
   Internet.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

NOV*IX for Internet V1.0 is available now.

