WAIS, Inc.'s WAISserver 2.0 For Alpha Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

*  WAIS, Inc. and Digital have entered into a marketing agreement
*  WAIS, Inc.'s WAISserver 2.0 software provides network publishing and text
   retrieval capabilities
*  WAISserver 2.0 is available now -- from WAIS, Inc. -- for Digital UNIX
   based systems, and will be available in September for Windows NT and in
   early 1996 for OpenVMS based Alpha systems

DESCRIPTION

WAIS, Inc. and Digital have entered into a marketing agreement that makes
WAIS network publishing and text retrieval software available to Digital
users.

WAIS, Inc is a software development company that has pioneered the online
publishing of information, especially via the Internet.  WAIS, Inc. develops
software products that help users find information by simply asking
questions in a natural language. The WAIS network publishing system creates
an open architecture of information servers and clients by using a standard
computer-to-computer protocol that enables clients to communicate with
servers.

The WAIS software architecture has four main components: the client, server,
database, and protocol.  The WAIS client is a user interface program that
sends search and retrieval requests to local or remote servers.  Clients are
available for most popular desktop environments.  The WAIS server is a
program that services client requests. The server software generally runs on
a server system containing one or more information sources or WAIS
databases.  The WAIS protocol, based on the National Information Standards
Organization (NISO) Z39.50 Information Retrieval Service and Protocol
Standard, is used to connect WAIS clients and servers.

WAISserver 2.0 Modules

WAIS Inc.'s WAISserver 2.0 includes eight major functional modules:

*  Search and retrieval software -- Search functionality for local and
   remote databases with relevance ranking and relevance feedback features.
*  Custom parser toolkit -- A customizable API (Application Programming
   Interface) for getting content from documents in any type of format.
*  Indexer -- Software for indexing local and remote content databases.
*  WAIS  Z39.50 Protocol Stack -- A protocol used to connect WAIS clients
   and servers.
*  WAISgate -- A gateway that converts the HTTP protocol used by the WWW to
   Z39.50 so that WWW servers and clients can initiate a WAIS search.
*  Gopher gateway  -- A gateway that converts Gopher protocol to Z39.50 so
   that Gopher servers and clients can initiate a WAIS search.
*  Forwarder -- Software that allows clients and servers separated by
   firewalls (security software) to access one another.
*  Management reporting -- Reports containing more than 20 statistics
   pertaining to users, usage patterns, connect time, and searches
   performed.

BENEFITS

*  Saves time and money by enabling the publishing of existing database
   information without costly HTML coding.
*  Increases user productivity by allowing users to seamlessly access local
   and remote databases.
*  Allows users choice in how they access information through support of
   popular desktop clients.
*  Minimizes start up and maintenance costs for an Internet-based service.
*  Enables the Internet publisher to plan better through tracking tools for
   usage and status.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

WAISserver 2.0 for Digital UNIX based systems is available now from WAIS,
Inc. To order the software, contact WAIS, Inc. via the Internet address,
digital@wais.com. WAISserver 2.0 will be available in September for Windows
NT based Alpha systems, and in early 1996 for OpenVMS based Alpha systems.

TECHNICAL DATA

Hardware and software prerequisites:

*  TCP/IP network to connect WAIS or WWW clients
*  Minimum of 32 MB of memory
*  5 MB of disk storage required for the WAIS software, plus additional
   storage capacity for indexes, which will take up about one-third the size
   of the current text database being served
