StorageWorks Raid Array 410 Enhancements

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Unequaled availability and performance through hot
   swappable, dual redundant, and active-active controllers
*  Increased performance and availability with support of RAID level 1
   (mirroring)
*  Support for 4 GB drives doubles capacity in Office Expansion RAID
   Enclosure to over 100 GB

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital's highly successful StorageWorks family now offers dual redundant
active-active controllers and RAID level 1 on the newest and highest
performance StorageWorks RAID Array 410 storage subsystem for Sun
SPARCstation servers, HP9000-800, and IBM RS6000 UNIX platforms. The RAID
Array 410 offers the ability to use RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, 3, and 5
concurrently to suit a variety of applications and performance requirements,
providing maximum data availability. The StorageWorks RAID Array 410 Office
Expansion RAID Enclosure now offers over 100 GB of disk storage with all the
StorageWorks features, including ease of serviceability and hot swapping of
all the redundant components (disks, fans, and power supplies). The dual
controllers are also hot swappable.

BENEFITS

Mission critical transaction processing database application environments
will realize maximum benefits with the addition of dual redundant
active-active controllers and RAID 1 support. Banking, communications,
insurance, health care, manufacturing, scientific, and research environments
will obtain highest availability with the RAID Array 410 through the
automatic sparing, redundancy, and hot swapping features.

A dual redundant active-active controller configuration is easily obtained
by adding a second hot pluggable controller to an existing RAID Array 410
and typing a few setup commands to specify workload distribution between the
active-active (shared workload) controllers. In the event of a controller
failure, the surviving controller will assume responsibility for the failed
controller's outstanding I/O operations and LUNS.

The RAID Array 410 system's mirroring feature (RAID level 1) will especially
benefit those users needing highest availability, and when combined with
RAID level 0 (striping), provides maximum performance of any RAID level
configuration. For client/server UNIX applications that demand high-end
performance with unequaled availability, the StorageWorks RAID Array 410
subsystem provides a complete, hardware-based, versatile, uniquely
affordable solution.

Users will welcome the addition of the 4 GB 7200 RPM disk drive as the
newest supported member of the RAID Array 410 family. The 4 GB drive doubles
capacity and enhances both throughput and bandwidth performance through its
high RPM and high bit density characteristics. Adding capacity and
customizing solutions are easier than ever before. Users need only determine
the capacity entry point they require and add capacity as needed just by
adding disk drives. StorageWorks RAID Array 410 pre-packaged configurations
come in 10 GB, 20 GB, or 40 GB sizes, and 1 GB, 2 GB, and 4 GB drives can be
added as they are required. (LUNs should be built using the same capacity
drives.) Users can also build their own capacity from Digital's Drive Ready
RAID Array 410 configurations.

Free Upgrades

Existing users of the RAID Array 410 system will receive free upgrades to
RAID Array 410 V2.5 firmware, which supports these new features. Users who
haven't been already contacted for the free upgrade may inquire through any
of these methods:

