Enhancements to Storage Library System for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha V2.5B

The Storage Library System for OpenVMS V2.5B supports OpenVMS VAX V6.2, and
OpenVMS Alpha V6.2 (SPD 29.67.11). In addition, the product continues to be
enhanced with support for TL820 controllers attached to HSJ40/HSD30
StorageWorks Array Controllers that are used with StorageWorks HS
Operating Firmware V2.5 controller. The following are new or changed
features in V2.5B:

*  A new option in the operator menu allows the volume database to be
   updated to specify that the tape volume is in a jukebox drive, rather
   than in a jukebox slot. The volume database can also be updated to
   specify that the tape volume is in a jukebox slot, rather than a jukebox
   drive.
*  A number of devices are now supported, including the TL820 through the
   HSJ and HSD controllers.
*  A new version of the Remote Device Facility (RDF) has been integrated.
*  Documentation enhancements and minor functionality additions.

V2.5B also corrects the following problems that existed in earlier versions:

*  Attempting to allocate a remote device occasionally returned an error
   indicating that all REDV devices were in use, even when not true.
*  Issuing a STORAGE LOAD command, followed by a CTRL-Y, caused an ACCVIO in
   the RQ process.
*  When a volume was in a magazine and the continue set was being used, the
   ALLOCDRIVE constructed failed.
*  On an Alpha system running OpenVMS V6.1, the following sequence of
   commands caused an ACCVIO:
   - $ ALLOCATE drive_name
   - $ STORAGE SELECT DRIVE drive_name
*  On an Alpha system running OpenVMS V6.1, a NODEVAVAL appeared when doing
   a STORAGE SELECT for a volume in robot.
*  When using the Odetics 5480 ACL, the drive loads and unloads occasionally
   did not wait long enough for the hardware to do the task.
*  In some instances, the Storage Library System failed to start up because
   the RDF startup tried to shutdown some UCX service.

