POLYCENTER Network Management Packages V3.0 for Europe

The POLYCENTER network management packages V3.0 are now available in Europe
with a 30-day lead time.  In adition, special pricing is now available for
DECmcc users.

The network management packages are preconfigured, factory-installed
hardware and software systems built around POLYCENTER NetView for Digital
UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) software, and shipped ready to run. Entry,
mid-range, and high-end packages are available for managing TCP/IP
networks, with optional DECnet management support (see the "POLYCENTER
Network Management Hardware and Software Packages V3.0" article in the April
1995 issue of Customer Update).

V3.0 packages are available using AlphaStation 200 and 400 PCI based
workstations. All systems are pre-configured with a CD-ROM reader, sound
card with headset, EIA 232 port, Ethernet, and a two-user Digital UNIX
license.

NOTE THAT TO GET A PACKAGE, TWO ORDER NUMBERS -- A CP-PNV**-** and a
QP-03***-** -- must be ordered. Each CP-PNV**-** order number includes
hardware, operating system, and  factory-installed software. Each
QP-*****-** order number includes the POLYCENTER layered products --
POLYCENTER NetView, PathDoctor, and DECnet Manager software -- which are
factory-installed. Order numbers with the -A*suffix are packages with DECnet
management support; those with the -D* suffix are packages with TCP/IP only
support. Hardware orders submitted without the specified QP-  part
numbers on the same order will be considered incomplete and will not be
processed.

Users ordering Digital UNIX based software for the first time are required
to purchase the DEC OSF/1 Media and Documentation and Software Library
CD-ROMs. Any additional software ordered will be shipped separately (not
pre-installed) and will not be included in the packaged system
discount.

